-- The file reader and writer read and write a `nupp.io.Buffer`'s storage
-- directly, by the `_data`, `_length` and `_capacity` fields the IO installer
-- above gives it. That coupling is deliberate: it is what lets a native read
-- land in the destination rather than in a Lua string on the way to it, and
-- both chunks are emitted together by one compiler into one program. A
-- destination without those fields still works, one copy slower.
